HU-MultiTenant - License for Use

Copyright (c) 2026 The authors of HU-MultiTenant. All rights reserved.

1. Permitted use
   The software "HU-MultiTenant" (program code, user interface, documentation,
   graphics) may be downloaded, installed and run free of charge - by
   private individuals, schools, public authorities, associations and
   companies. Copies for your own use (e.g. on USB drives, servers or
   shares of your own organization) are permitted.

2. Own settings, extensions and snippets
   The following is expressly permitted:
   a) adjusting the configuration files in the "Config" folder (e.g.
      settings.json, quick-snippets.json, update.json) through the program
      or a text editor,
   b) creating, using and sharing your own extensions (new files in the
      "Extensions" folder, e.g. based on Extensions\Template.ps1) and your
      own Quick Script snippets. They belong to their authors and are not
      covered by section 3.

3. Not permitted (without prior written consent of the authors)
   a) to modify, adapt or translate the program code or the documentation,
      or to incorporate any part of it into other software,
   b) to use or distribute modified versions,
   c) to sell or rent the software, or to offer it for a fee as part of a
      product or service,
   d) to publish the software outside the official repository
      (distribution within your own organization is permitted),
   e) to remove or alter copyright, license or version notices.

4. GitHub
   Viewing and forking the repository within the GitHub Terms of Service
   remains unaffected. A fork does not grant any of the rights listed
   under section 3.

5. Warranty and liability
   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the
   extent permitted by law, the authors are not liable for any damage,
   data loss or consequential damage arising from its use - in particular
   not for changes made to Microsoft 365 tenants by extensions or scripts.
   Check write actions with DRY-RUN first.

6. Final provisions
   This license is governed by Austrian law. Should any provision be
   invalid, the remaining provisions shall remain in effect.
